ent and reduce costs for key hybrid cloud storage use cases. These include =
moving backups to the cloud, using on-premises file shares backed by cloud =
storage, and providing low latency access to data in AWS for on-premises ap=
plications.</p>

<p><strong>AWS Snowball</strong> - AWS Snowball is a physical data transpor=
t device used for large-scale offline data transfers. It is ideal when you =
need to migrate terabytes or petabytes of data and lack high-speed internet=
. However, it is not an online or ongoing transfer solution, nor does it su=
pport automated or incremental backups.</p>

<p><strong>AWS Snowball Edge</strong> - AWS Snowball Edge is an enhanced ve=
rsion of AWS Snowball that supports local compute capabilities in addition =
to offline data transfers. It is suitable for edge computing and disconnect=
ed environments, not for ongoing online data transfers with incremental syn=
c.</p>

